 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "n-land",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-land",
   "text": "First, because it is the first thing anyone meets \u2014 and <b>every row below is one screen at both widths</b>: 1440 light, 360 light, 1440 dark, 360 dark. Built from real components at their real size, fragments rather than whole screens, and on the 1440 board from the WEB app's own components, because a laptop reader must see the tables and the dashboard they will actually get. <b>First launch</b> is the screen an <i>installed</i> app shows: v1 is a PWA (spec \u00a7G, <i>the app is installable</i>), and an installed app opens cold \u2014 no address bar, no landing page, nothing to have scrolled. It is not a mobile screen; it is what any installed copy shows on a device with no budget on it yet. `LandMotion` draws the pointer states, because a static artboard cannot show motion and the build cannot implement from a description. Two image slots are specified and not filled \u2014 `docs/design/image-brief.md` carries the shot list, the licences and the reject list."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-w-in",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-in",
   "text": "The whole account flow, then the six setting-up steps, <b>every screen on its own row at both widths</b> \u2014 because a six-step flow drawn as one picture is a picture, not a flow, and two widths on separate pages is how they drift. They did: the 1440 steps were wrong on four of six, and the 360 screen had each of those four right the whole time. <b>Sign-up no longer carries a trust panel.</b> It carries the one fixed claim (tokens \u00a710.1) and a link that opens security and privacy as a modal \u2014 one copy of the wording instead of five \u2014 plus an explicit tick-box, because consent you have to tick is consent and a sentence above a button is not. <i>Forgot password</i> and <i>Reset password</i> are three screens, not one \u2014 ask, wait, set \u2014 because the step in the middle is where resets actually fail. The three 360-only rows are sheets a phone needs and a laptop does not."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-w-home",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-home",
   "text": "Home and its states, each at both widths on one row. The width holds the workings: the figure and its pace card left, the reason \u2014 where the money is, then every category worst-first \u2014 right, and reading one against the other is exactly what 360 cannot do. <b>The gauge lives at 360 only</b>, because <i>can I spend this, right now?</i> is asked in a shop with a phone in your hand; at a desk the question is whether you are on pace, and a dial has no memory of yesterday. Each state is its own row because each has its own fix."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-w-money",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-money",
   "text": "The month's money, both widths per row. Transactions gets a standing filter rail and real columns at 1440 \u2014 stacked filters scroll the list away, and losing your place is the one thing that matters here \u2014 and tabs at 360, where they earn their place. Debts loses its tabs entirely at 1440, because the best thing width buys is sometimes one less control. Both empty states of Transactions are separate rows: one wants a movement, the other wants the filters cleared. Opening balances and debts are dated 24 September, the day before the cycle, so they never count as this cycle's saving."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-w-acct",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-acct",
   "text": "What an account is for, the three screens the paid tier exists to serve, and the import flow \u2014 spec \u00a77.9, the most dangerous action in the app. <b>There is no lock anywhere on this page</b>: no padlock, no grey-out, no crown, and the word <i>unlock</i> appears nowhere (item 24, and the build guard checks it). Reconciliation is one movement at a time, never a list of forms. The household disagreement is two people agreeing, not software refereeing: both figures drawn as equals, no rose, and <i>leave it for now</i> the same weight as the rest. Every import refusal ends with \u201cNothing has changed.\u201d and none of them is red \u2014 the file was wrong, the person was not."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-brand",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-brand",
   "text": "The mark is the mizan beam \u2014 a set of scales, tipped, because the app exists to say whether today is in balance. Locked. It is the app icon, the favicon, the sidebar lockup and the letterhead on the printed debt record."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-found",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-found",
   "text": "The primitives sheet \u2014 every component in every state, both themes \u2014 then the palette and type tile, and the printed debt record: A4, black and white, no app chrome, because it leaves the app and is read by someone who was never in it."
  }
 ],
